#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d7b5b60-5d79-5ecc-885d-672aa36b618e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336444} {:answer/id #uuid "db1c848e-7039-524b-acec-7a97638ea8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336445} {:answer/id #uuid "15242d95-73d8-5103-8d28-5c5ecbf4876a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336446} {:answer/id #uuid "c6310a41-f731-5a59-a52f-533767178a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336447} {:answer/id #uuid "935a127c-722d-521b-822a-cb8eb1cddcd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6310a41-f731-5a59-a52f-533767178a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336447} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d1f3586-e488-59a6-807e-47f720662ab1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "896ad5f4-5c0f-5568-aae4-0aa7b71a3f60" :question/math-academy-id "q-124321" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v-u+2,\\,y=2u+v-5.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-5$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v-u+2 \\\\ 2u+v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "36996ffc-7dbc-51f8-8efe-46ed2c897045" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether an Affine Transformation is Orientation-Preserving"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbd3b259-5668-50ef-82ed-c5569de8b013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336451} {:answer/id #uuid "50bb5287-4f92-5cd8-9ad3-2e50d97c0eeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336452} {:answer/id #uuid "f4f6b4d7-f633-58bd-a906-aa62ddef3259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336453} {:answer/id #uuid "557cd5c5-92ab-52c9-a384-fbf352fbc28a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336454} {:answer/id #uuid "4aeebe64-a0a2-5aec-8544-3012c052996f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbd3b259-5668-50ef-82ed-c5569de8b013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336451} :answer-field/id #uuid "43a4746c-2758-5329-971d-cabb39add107" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4476f995-ba26-5b0c-8399-063838391faa" :question/math-academy-id "q-124324" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u-3v-5,\\,y=-2u+2v+4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=2$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v-5 \\\\ -2u+2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-3v \\\\ -2u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|=4\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-2)=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336456 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fd0b67f-681b-5b1d-8be9-2ab2d1ca5e66" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Polygon Under an Affine Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de60bbe-937d-5966-8a97-d2e7b10e61db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/741501ec388180aca96136e286f1e871eeaa4e89c3ad36558fd5a384e6951001.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336458} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1e7534-8f92-5a8e-9e45-2b71f1c981d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/01ddff6313a9f86ad9cb750a23f65900f7031afef2f30826efecba379064f3f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336459} {:answer/id #uuid "a91cdc39-aca0-5c0b-bff8-060059f26332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/c297c5a3c483cacf056d9765bca2e31d8056c157d334c2f1571e775cf671e579.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336460} {:answer/id #uuid "c7fd8001-db07-5610-927e-fc5f084f19be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/93b061334bdf3b55345bd8e42bf9003f75d9f9221cd8b45d738f3c2bb1523d3a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336461} {:answer/id #uuid "de8dfb1f-6cfa-50f6-a9a9-a918c82d7335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/4762d50ba86ed040fa1021afdedde9a7d23c873b2a8f5f434752f6e69af2bbb7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0de60bbe-937d-5966-8a97-d2e7b10e61db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/741501ec388180aca96136e286f1e871eeaa4e89c3ad36558fd5a384e6951001.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336458} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb018dd4-24e9-5ce4-b449-d83965268cc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f247c61f-a32a-51c8-8ab7-d1810efeb527" :question/math-academy-id "q-124558" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/43eb119ef43e136682d4451e4f85f007c63568f7a34880c46f87ab45122f5dd0.png)\n\nConsider the rectangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=1-u,\\,y=2-v.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-u \\\\ 2-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/a8a13c579c3ca8cc32f997c48e237c38d449aa07040de658589fa5cc68a02c55.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(2,2),(-1,2),(-1,1),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14056028/assets/146f9f36deeac0f3a7108a173485eb6d0d03138d18998a96dc9c3566bee21ca2.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=1>0,$ this transformation is orientation-preserving."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area Scale Factor of an Affine Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8d6e23-7d03-5eed-8692-bb8f8662b858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336465} {:answer/id #uuid "e61a4983-134d-5cc1-9658-47210bceb884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336466} {:answer/id #uuid "ec60ce9c-7411-5ce6-9bc8-0df814647935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336467} {:answer/id #uuid "569c44ff-3667-5223-8904-553fcc7e074a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336468} {:answer/id #uuid "146f481d-f4d2-5478-950b-954a0bfc94f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "146f481d-f4d2-5478-950b-954a0bfc94f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336469} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa90a36f-be39-596e-a305-9f410c10aa84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ea3d1aa-9c05-5567-8f1e-1380bcadd18c" :question/math-academy-id "q-162188" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+v-2,\\,y=u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v-2 \\\\ u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 1=-4.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-4|=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1577f765-f98c-5020-8e45-8da2c5f092e6" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area Scale Factor of an Affine Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac4709bb-e78f-5ed0-a54d-20bc80db1d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336472} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf8126d-fe66-5090-bbd1-bd4bf5f6ba72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336473} {:answer/id #uuid "6b88523e-430b-57b9-9da1-4a0aad5856db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336474} {:answer/id #uuid "a179170c-727e-57b9-a770-0af187f200ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336475} {:answer/id #uuid "874a61eb-d97b-522d-bf81-57fa865faf51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac4709bb-e78f-5ed0-a54d-20bc80db1d08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336472} :answer-field/id #uuid "22040642-5c60-59ff-aff2-c87bf4273d23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336471}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a97213e8-47eb-5b89-aef9-04a62f82dcf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-162190" :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=2v-u-5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 2v-u-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ -u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|3|=3.\n$$"}]}
